# The sdist is the archival artifact: it should contain what a reader needs to audit the
# release, not just what is importable. setuptools' defaults pick up `tests/test_*.py` but
# miss `tests/__init__.py` (so the test package arrives incomplete), and skip the docs the
# README links to and the citation metadata.
include CITATION.cff
include CHANGELOG.md
include CONTRIBUTING.md
include NOTICE
include tests/__init__.py
include tests/TESTS.md
recursive-include docs *.md
# The decision notebooks are the evidence behind the defaults in decisions.yaml, which is
# exactly what "audit the release" means for this package. Non-recursive on purpose:
# notebooks/ also holds a gitignored on-disk cache and, once either notebook has been opened
# in Jupyter, a .ipynb_checkpoints/ copy -- and an sdist is built from the working tree, not
# from git, so `recursive-include ... *.ipynb` would ship a stale checkpoint of the notebook
# beside the real one.
include notebooks/*.ipynb
